            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So this doesn't look at all feasible, unfortunately.\r\n\r\nThe clang-analyzer failure is actually unrelated, but surfaces now that the macros are inlined on Linux as well so that the full code is analyzed:\r\n```\r\n/home/runner/work/neovim/neovim/src/nvim/buffer.c:162:40: error: Division by zero [clang-analyzer-core.DivideZero,-warnings-as-errors]\r\n  162 |   return (part > 1000000) ? (int)(part / (whole / 100))\r\n      |                                        ^\r\n```\r\nFor this to actually occur, you need to have a buffer with one line, which has line number 1000000 -- which obviously will never happen in Neovim. If we wanted to silence the warning, the cleanest way would be to add an `assert` against this situation before it.\r\n\r\n(Leaving this here in case it crops up again and someone searches for the error; all credit to @dundargoc for investigating this.)",
